# AM01 FPGA programming (am01-fpga.service)
#
# Loads /boot/am01.bit into the Kintex-7 with openFPGALoader, over a USB-JTAG
# adapter plugged into the CM4. Nothing happens unless that file exists, so
# programming the board externally over JTAG remains an option.
#
# FPGA_OPTS must name your adapter -- there is no safe default. List what is
# connected with:
#
#   openFPGALoader --scan-usb
#
# Then set the cable, for example:
#
#   FPGA_OPTS="-c ft2232"        # generic FT2232-based adapter
#   FPGA_OPTS="-c digilent"      # Digilent HS2/HS3
#   FPGA_OPTS="-c xvc-client"    # Xilinx Virtual Cable
#
# Add -f to write the bitstream to flash instead of loading it into SRAM;
# without -f the FPGA loses its configuration on power-down and this unit
# reloads it on each boot.
FPGA_OPTS=""

# Check it by hand before enabling the service:
#   openFPGALoader $FPGA_OPTS /boot/am01.bit
